  <section>
    <h2>Evidence</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Galaxy Rotation Curves</h3>
        <pre><code>v(r) = √(GM(r)/r)
Keplerian: v ∝ 1/√r at large r
Observation: v ≈ const at large r
Implies M(r) ∝ r (dark matter halo)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gravitational Lensing</h3>
        <pre><code>Massive objects bend light
Lensing strength ∝ enclosed mass
Cluster lensing reveals dark matter
Bullet Cluster: dark matter separated from gas</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Candidates</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>WIMPs</h3>
        <pre><code>Weakly Interacting Massive Particles
Mass: ~ 10-1000 GeV/c²
Interaction: weak force
Detection: nuclear recoils
Status: no detection yet</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Other Candidates</h3>
        <pre><code>Axions: very light, strong B field detection
Sterile neutrinos: keV mass range
MACHOs: brown dwarfs, black holes (ruled out)
Primordial black holes: varying mass range
Fuzzy dark matter: ultralight scalar field</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Detection Methods</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Direct Detection</h3>
        <pre><code>Underground detectors (low background)
Nuclear recoils from WIMP scattering
XENON, LUX, PandaX experiments
Annual modulation: Earth's velocity through halo
Status: no confirmed detection</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Indirect Detection</h3>
        <pre><code>Dark matter annihilation/decay products
Gamma rays: Fermi-LAT, H.E.S.S.
Neutrinos: IceCube
Antimatter: AMS-02
Status: some unconfirmed signals</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

